  ],
  "text": "Take the sea otters away and the entire kelp forest is gone within a few years. Otters do not eat kelp. They never touch the stuff. They eat urchins. And urchins eat kelp, constantly, forever. So no otters means unlimited urchins, and unlimited urchins means bare rock. It runs the other way too. A beaver builds the pond everything else needs. Elephants knock trees over, and that is what keeps a savannah open. And none of it has anything to do with how many of them there are. A rare species can be holding the structure up. A common one often is not. Which is why losing one animal is sometimes losing everything above it. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
